Z||000000||MooCow||09-06-2000||11:56 AM||||What kind of leak do I have now?? It smells like antifreeze but I have it inside the car.  I went and switched over from my Fiero to my Ranger for the winter and when taking the deck out I seen that the back of the cord on the deck were wet.  I smelled it and it was antifreeze!  I looked back there and seen that everything behind the dash where the deck goes was wet and even on the floor onb teh passenger side had a little puddle of it!  Where is this comming from cause I checked the antifreeze container up front and it was okay.  Please help before I put her in storage behind my house.<P>                        Thanks Ken||||reg||11
Z||000001||theogre||09-06-2000||12:03 PM||||heater core let go. buy a new one. about $50 for the part and about 45 minutes to an hour to instal it. No special tools needed.||||reg||1
Z||000002||mshill||09-06-2000||12:09 PM||||MooCow,  see your other post.  I just responded.  If you are going to fix the heater core and the radiator, go ahead and put out another $40-50 and replace all the hoses that you can get.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Oreif||09-06-2000||12:14 PM||||Heater core is bad. I bet on the passenger side of your windsheild just above the defroster vent has an oily film on it. Not too bad to replace, Just make sure you refill the cooling system properly when you are done to avoid air pockets. ||||reg||1
Z||000004||StuGood||09-06-2000||01:10 PM||||Okay - I hate to disagree with you guys, but personally, I think it's the heater core.<P>But you were <B>close</B> - ! ||||reg||12
Z||000005||MooCow||09-06-2000||02:28 PM||||Can I just simply wait until after winter to fix it?? I don't want to have to deeal with my car till next year now so I already put it up for the winter in my backyard.  Can't I just buy antifreeze and keep it filled up everytime I start it up?  So then my radiator is not blown nor has a leak??  I still get a little puddle of antifreeze under the car so is it still from the heater core??<P>                               Thanks Ken||||reg||5
Z||000006||Gold-86SE||09-06-2000||04:00 PM||||<BR>You can wait to replace your heater core.  However, if you are going to start the car during the winter you really should loop the hoses that connect to the heater core itself.  Looping the hoses will prevent coolant loss.<P>Now, if you want heat in the cabin while you are running the fiero during the winter replace that heater core.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Gold-86SE (Fiero Collector)||||reg||1
Z||000007||JohnnyK||09-06-2000||04:03 PM||||Ya, you should loop the hoses so that it's not leaking in there when you run the car, but to do that, you have to get in there, and might as well replace it anyways.||||reg||1
Z||000008||theogre||09-06-2000||05:32 PM||||Your leak on the ground depends just where under the car it is. if it's back under the cabin it's probly the heater core leaking water out the AC drain. If it's up front you have more problems.||||reg||1
